{
  "dom_id": "step-q211448",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Expressed as a whole number, $6÷\\frac{3}{4}=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $6$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n6=\\frac{6}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{3}{4}$ is $\\frac{4}{3}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n6÷\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{6}{1}÷\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{4}{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{6\\times 4}{1\\times 3}=\\frac{24}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n24÷3=8\n$$",
